  "title": "Testimony from 40 Faithful Believers",
  "data": "Through a valid chain of narrators, Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said, “When a faithful believer dies and forty faithful believers attend his funeral and say these words about him, Almighty Allah will say to them: I have accepted your testimony, and I forgive him what you do not know about him but I do:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنَّا لَا نَعْلَمُ مِنْهُ اِلَّا خَيْرًا وَاَنْتَ اَعْلَمُ بِهٖ مِنَّا\nALLAAHUMMA INNAA LAA NA'LAMU MINHU ILLAA KHAYRAN WA ANTA A'LAMU BIHEE MINNAA\nO Allah, we know nothing of him but good, and You know him better than we do.\nAccording to another validly reported tradition, the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said, “The first heading in a faithful believer's record of deeds is what people say about him after his death. If they say good things, his record is good; but if they say evil things, his record is evil.”"
}
